                <pb facs="1065" n="1059" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1059"/>

                <head>No. 10.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Liliuokalani to Mr. Damon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                31, 1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. S. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Damon</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Honolulu:</hi></p>
                <p>Sir: You having stated that, as a condition upon which you would only authorize
                    the lending by your firm of Bishop &amp; Co. to me of the further sum of
                    $10,000, upon certain securities that I need not specify, I should hand to you
                    the original new constitution that it was my intention to promulgate on the day
                    of the prorogation of the late Legislature, January 14, 1893, I assure you that
                    I am unable to comply with such condition, for the sole reason that such new
                    constitution and all copies thereof and the draft thereof have been destroyed,
                    the original constitution by my own hands and the copies thereof and the draft
                    by my orders.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Liliuokalani.</hi></signed><lb/><salute>In presence
                            of—</salute><lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul
                        Neumann</hi></signed>,<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry
                            Holmes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
